## The wave loop

```
read inbox -> claim next row from queue/{x}.md -> build -> prove by artifact (no tests — line 3)
  -> commit (explicit pathspec, -F message file, judge by `git log -1` grep of the marker)
  -> write evidence/{x}/<row>-<fresh-name>.* -> post VERIFY -> post STATUS -> repeat
```

Read the inbox at the **top of every row** and **after every VERIFY**. Post on state change,
not on a schedule.

### Your commit marker — fixed format, not a choice

Every commit you make carries this marker on its **first line**:

```
[run-{NN}][lane-{x}][<row-id>] <subject>
```

That exact string is what mandatory line 1 tells you to grep for in `git log -1`, and it is
what the gate's conformance check reads to prove the gate lane built nothing. A commit without
it did not happen, as far as this run is concerned. Write it into the `-F` message file; do not
type it on the command line.

## Tests — not yours

You do not run tests (line 3; fleet-ops rule 10). If a row's order asks for a test, write it,
commit it with the row, and leave it unrun — the HQ merge gate is its first run. Your proof of
the row is the artifact under `evidence/{x}/`: the rendered page, the query result, the curl
body, the diff. A test written to produce a PASS line is a defect.
`npx <tool>` is FORBIDDEN if `<tool>` appears anywhere in `package.json`; use `npm run …` or
`node_modules\.bin\…` (build tools only).

